<form class="standard-form dmc-journal-transfer-form">
	<section class="dmc-transfer-section">
		<header>
			<h2>Journal Text to Subsystem Export</h2>
			<p>Paste plain text copied from a journal entry and convert it into a PF2e subsystem export file. The parser can recognize influence, research, and infiltration style text.</p>
		</header>
		<p class="hint">Recommended workflow: copy the journal text, paste it into Journal Text, click Preview Export JSON to sanity-check the result, then click Download Subsystem Export to save the file to your computer.</p>
		<div class="dmc-transfer-actions">
			<button type="button" data-action="preview-journal-json">
				<i class="fas fa-eye"></i> Preview Export JSON
			</button>
			{{#if subsystemsEnabled}}
			<button type="button" data-action="create-live-subsystem">
				<i class="fas fa-plus"></i> Create Live Subsystem
			</button>
			{{/if}}
			<button type="button" data-action="export-journal-text">
				<i class="fas fa-download"></i> Download Subsystem Export
			</button>
		</div>
		{{#if subsystemsEnabled}}
		<p class="hint">Create Live Subsystem sends the parsed result directly into PF2e Subsystems as a new editable live entry instead of downloading a file.</p>
		{{else}}
		<p class="hint">Enable the PF2e Subsystems module to create live subsystem entries directly from this window.</p>
		{{/if}}
		<label class="dmc-transfer-textarea">
			<span>Journal Text</span>
			<textarea name="journalText" spellcheck="false">{{journalText}}</textarea>
		</label>
		<label class="dmc-transfer-textarea">
			<span>Generated Export JSON</span>
			<textarea name="journalJson" spellcheck="false" readonly></textarea>
		</label>
	</section>
	<section class="dmc-transfer-section">
		<header>
			<h2>Generate New Subsystem</h2>
			<p>Build a fresh subsystem event from curated PF2e-flavored prompts. The generator uses the party's average level as the default, applies the GM Core level-based DC table, and varies checks slightly around that baseline.</p>
		</header>
		<p class="hint">Use this when you want a ready-to-edit starting point instead of copying from a journal. Generated checks only use Pathfinder 2e skills and common Lore skills.</p>
		<div class="dmc-generator-fields">
			<label>
				<span>Subsystem Type</span>
				<select name="generatedType">
					{{#each generatorTypes}}
					<option value="{{this.value}}">{{this.label}}</option>
					{{/each}}
				</select>
			</label>
			<label>
				<span>Name</span>
				<input type="text" name="generatedName" value="{{generatedName}}" placeholder="Optional custom name">
			</label>
			<label>
				<span>Level</span>
				<input type="number" name="generatedLevel" value="{{generatedLevel}}" min="-1" max="26" step="1">
			</label>
		</div>
		<div class="dmc-transfer-actions">
			<button type="button" data-action="preview-generated-json">
				<i class="fas fa-wand-magic-sparkles"></i> Preview Generated JSON
			</button>
			{{#if subsystemsEnabled}}
			<button type="button" data-action="create-generated-live-subsystem">
				<i class="fas fa-plus"></i> Create Live Generated Subsystem
			</button>
			{{/if}}
			<button type="button" data-action="download-generated-subsystem">
				<i class="fas fa-download"></i> Download Generated Export
			</button>
		</div>
		{{#if subsystemsEnabled}}
		<p class="hint">Create Live Generated Subsystem sends the generated event directly into PF2e Subsystems as a new editable live entry.</p>
		{{else}}
		<p class="hint">Enable the PF2e Subsystems module to create generated subsystem entries directly from this window.</p>
		{{/if}}
		<label class="dmc-transfer-textarea">
			<span>Generated Subsystem JSON</span>
			<textarea name="generatedJson" spellcheck="false" readonly></textarea>
		</label>
	</section>
</form>
